# Validation 4: partition then reconnection scenario.
# Two clusters {0,1,2,3} and {4,5,6,7} connected by a single bridge link
# 3-4. The bridge goes down for a while, then comes back. All cross-cluster
# packets are timed when the bridge is up (per the spec reachability
# guarantee). Intra-cluster packets are scheduled during the partition.
NODES 8

# Left cluster: 0-1-2-3 mesh
EDGE 0 1 2
EDGE 0 2 3
EDGE 1 2 2
EDGE 1 3 3
EDGE 2 3 4

# Right cluster: 4-5-6-7 mesh
EDGE 4 5 2
EDGE 4 6 3
EDGE 5 6 2
EDGE 5 7 3
EDGE 6 7 4

# Bridge
EDGE 3 4 10

# --- Phase 1: bridge up ---
T 100 PKT 0 7
T 200 PKT 5 1
T 300 PKT 2 6

# --- Bridge goes down at T=500 ---
T 500 LINK 3 4 -1

# --- Phase 2: bridge down, only intra-cluster traffic ---
T 600 PKT 0 2
T 700 PKT 5 7
T 800 PKT 1 3
T 900 PKT 4 6

# --- Bridge comes back at T=1200 (with new cost) ---
T 1200 LINK 3 4 5

# --- Phase 3: bridge back up, cross-cluster traffic resumes ---
T 1400 PKT 0 7
T 1500 PKT 6 1
T 1700 PKT 2 5
T 1900 PKT 7 3
